grammar:{title:"El se dativo ético y enfático",explain:"Spanish adds pronouns for flavor. Enfático with consumption verbs: «Se comió TODA la pizza» (polished it off) vs plain «Comió pizza». Dativo ético shows who's affected: «No me le grites al niño» (don't yell at MY kid), «Se me marchitó la planta» (my plant wilted on me). These little pronouns carry emotion.",examples:[
{es:"El perro se comió las semillas enteritas.",en:"The dog ate up every last seed."},
{es:"Se me secó el huerto en las vacaciones.",en:"My garden dried up on me during vacation."},
{es:"No me le eches tanta agua a la sábila.",en:"Don't overwater my aloe (I care about it)."}],
exercises:[
{q:"«___ tomó todo el jugo de un trago.» (emphatic)",options:["Se","Le","Lo","Nos"],a:0,hint:"Se + consumption verb = polished it off."},
{q:"«Se ___ murió la planta.» (on me)",options:["me","le","lo","te"],a:0,hint:"Affected person → me."},
{q:"«No me ___ des dulces al niño.»",options:["le","lo","se","la"],a:0,hint:"Dativo ético: me (my interest) + le (to the kid)."},
{q:"«Se ___ marchitaron las rosas a Lupita.»",options:["le","les","la","me"],a:0,hint:"To Lupita (singular) → le."}]},
